packaging/ — upstream packaging seeds
=====================================

This directory is NOT a debian/ directory and the tree builds no .deb packages.
It holds the per-package metadata that imud maintains upstream so that real
packaging (a self-hosted apt repository first, Debian inclusion eventually)
is mechanical when it starts. One subdirectory per binary package:

  imud/            the core daemon + tools (imud, imud-cal, imud-status, imud-mon)
  libimud/         client shared library (future split: libimud0 + libimud-dev)
  imud-signalk/    Signal K bridge
  imud-mqtt/       MQTT bridge (links libmosquitto)
  imud-influxdb/   InfluxDB bridge
  imud-mavlink/    MAVLink bridge

The four bridges link libimud at runtime, so as .debs they will
Depend: libimud0 (built from this same source).

Each contains:

  copyright     DEP-5 machine-readable copyright (becomes debian/copyright)
  changelog     release history in Debian changelog format (see note below)
  description   synopsis + long description (seeds debian/control Description:)

`make install` / `make install-<bridge>` install copyright and changelog.gz
into /usr/share/doc/<pkg>/ so even a plain `make install` follows Debian doc
conventions.

Notes for the future packager
-----------------------------

* Versions in the changelogs are currently NATIVE format ("1.2"). When real
  Debian packaging starts, the package should be NON-native: version "1.2-1",
  built from the upstream tarball `make dist` produces
  (imud-1.2.tar.gz -> imud_1.2.orig.tar.gz). The changelogs here then continue
  as the upstream release notes, and debian/changelog tracks packaging
  revisions separately.
* Build with the packaging paths:
      make PREFIX=/usr SVCDIR=/lib/systemd/system DESTDIR=<stage> install
  When DESTDIR is set, the install is a pure file copy: no useradd and no
  systemctl calls — user creation and daemon-reload belong in the package's
  maintainer scripts (the `imud` system user needs the gpio and i2c groups;
  imud-mavlink's serial output additionally wants dialout).
* systemd units are generated from etc/*.service.in with the real bin dir
  substituted for @BINDIR@; they land in $(SVCDIR).
* Configs in /etc/imud/ are installed non-clobbering by make; as .debs they
  should be conffiles (shipped verbatim from config/*.conf).
* CFLAGS/CPPFLAGS/LDFLAGS from the environment (dpkg-buildflags) are
  respected; mandatory flags are appended with `override +=` so hardening
  injection works on every binary.
* libimud's SONAME is libimud.so.0 and its data struct is append-only; only a
  (never planned lightly) breaking ABI change bumps the SONAME and the
  runtime package name (libimud0 → libimud1). See docs/RELEASING.md.
* The upstream release tag convention is vX.Y (see docs/RELEASING.md).
